[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3156802990","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109343#issuecomment-3156802990","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109343","id":3156802990,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc68KP2u","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-05T22:15:27Z","updated_at":"2025-08-05T22:15:27Z","body":"I've been able to get https://github.com/Calinou/slippi-hitsounds working with official Godot binaries (which always use `builtin_enet=yes`). This project communicates with a locally running [Slippi](https://slippi.gg/) instance which uses ENet, so I'm also using its official Linux binaries on that side.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3156802990/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3159045621","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109343#issuecomment-3159045621","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109343","id":3159045621,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc68SzX1","user":{"login":"beaverxsheet","id":39215390,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5MjE1Mzkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39215390?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/beaverxsheet","html_url":"https://github.com/beaverxsheet","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beaverxsheet/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beaverxsheet/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beaverxsheet/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beaverxsheet/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beaverxsheet/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beaverxsheet/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beaverxsheet/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beaverxsheet/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beaverxsheet/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-06T10:07:13Z","updated_at":"2025-08-06T10:09:10Z","body":"I currently can't test that with Slippi, but I have looked into Slippis source for the place where connections are initialized. As far as I can tell `SlippiSpectateServer::SlippicommSocketThread()` in `SlippiSpectate.cpp` (in https://github.com/project-slippi/Ishiiruka) contains the logic for connecting new clients. To me that all looks pretty similar to what I am doing in my `server.c` (in the package.zip).","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3159045621/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3273492991","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109343#issuecomment-3273492991","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109343","id":3273492991,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7DHYn_","user":{"login":"kilometer3604","id":899899,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5OTg5OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/899899?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilometer3604","html_url":"https://github.com/kilometer3604","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilometer3604/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilometer3604/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilometer3604/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilometer3604/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilometer3604/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilometer3604/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilometer3604/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilometer3604/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilometer3604/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-10T06:30:19Z","updated_at":"2025-09-10T06:32:37Z","body":"The following GDScript  client code works for me (Godot 4.4.1):\n```gdscript\nextends Node\n\nvar IP_ADDRESS = \"127.0.0.1\"\nvar PORT = 9000\n\nvar enet\n\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n    enet = ENetConnection.new()\n\n    var error = enet.create_host(1, 2)\n    if error:\n        print(error_string(error))\n\n    var peer = enet.connect_to_host(IP_ADDRESS, PORT, 2)\n    if not peer:\n        print(\"Failed to get enet peer\")\n\n    var e\n\n    # Send connect request. Cannot receive any response (VERIFY_CONNECT) from server even using 10 seconds timeout. Not sure why.\n    e = enet.service(1000)\n    print(e[0], e[1], e[2], e[3])  # Prints \"0<Object#null>00\"\n\n    # Receive VERIFY_CONNECT from server\n    e = enet.service(1000)\n    print(e[0], e[1], e[2], e[3])  # Prints \"1<ENetPacketPeer#-9223372006790003365>00\"\n\n    # Send ACK back to server to establish connection\n    e = enet.service(1000)\n    print(e[0], e[1], e[2], e[3])  # Prints \"0<Object#null>00\"\n```\n\nBut if using a vanilla enet client written is C, only two calls of `enet_host_service()` are needed.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3273492991/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3273653607","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109343#issuecomment-3273653607","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109343","id":3273653607,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7DH_1n","user":{"login":"kilometer3604","id":899899,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5OTg5OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/899899?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilometer3604","html_url":"https://github.com/kilometer3604","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilometer3604/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilometer3604/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilometer3604/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilometer3604/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilometer3604/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilometer3604/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilometer3604/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilometer3604/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilometer3604/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-10T07:20:32Z","updated_at":"2025-09-10T07:20:32Z","body":"It seems the `enet_host_service()` function in Godot does nothing but waiting for the timeout in [this loop](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/2dd26a027a99633231184616d4dd287bbdd1c0a3/thirdparty/enet/protocol.c#L1899), because the built-in [enet_socket_wait()](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/2dd26a027a99633231184616d4dd287bbdd1c0a3/thirdparty/enet/enet_godot.cpp#L577) has an empty implementation and always returns 0.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3273653607/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3313019633","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109343#issuecomment-3313019633","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109343","id":3313019633,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7FeKrx","user":{"login":"beaverxsheet","id":39215390,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5MjE1Mzkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39215390?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/beaverxsheet","html_url":"https://github.com/beaverxsheet","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beaverxsheet/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beaverxsheet/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beaverxsheet/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beaverxsheet/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beaverxsheet/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beaverxsheet/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beaverxsheet/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beaverxsheet/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beaverxsheet/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-19T17:11:40Z","updated_at":"2025-09-19T17:11:40Z","body":"I've managed to get ENet working with the Godot implementation by adding a bypass in `enet_socket_wait()` which was blocking the loop from exiting as mentioned before. I haven't tested it with other implementations added by Godot yet (i.e. the implementation for DTLS) so that still might be an issue.\n\nThe fix is here #110697.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3313019633/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]